{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"adjudication":"Root reviewed the displayed task, definedness and stated conventional interpretation.","derivedAnswer":"C, 17865","reason":"With k repeated digits, a=8(10^k-1)/9 and b=5(10^k-1)/9, so 9ab=40(10^k-1)^2/9. A verified decimal expansion is k-1 copies of 4, then 3, then k-1 copies of 5, then 60. In powers of ten it is 4*sum(10^j,j=k+2..2k)+3*10^(k+1)+5*sum(10^j,j=2..k)+60; the two geometric sums give exactly the preceding product. Its digit sum is 4(k-1)+3+5(k-1)+6=9k=17865. Empty sums make the formula valid at k=1 too.","recordedAnswer":"C","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1985_AMC_12_Q29","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p096","cnm_p116"],"id":"decimal-block-subtraction","label":"Subtract in decimal blocks","methodDirectNodeIds":{"decimal-block-subtraction":["math:repdigit-product-digits"]},"nodeIds":["math:repdigit-product-digits","cnm_p096","cnm_p116"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A, 846","reason":"If R is the 94-digit string of fours, the product is R·10^94-R. Its digits are 93 fours followed by 3, then 93 fives followed by 6. Their sum is 93(4+5)+3+6=846.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1994_AMC_8_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_019","cnm_p116"],"id":"decimal-block-subtraction","label":"Multiply by a power of ten, then subtract","methodDirectNodeIds":{"decimal-block-subtraction":["math:repdigit-product-digits"]},"nodeIds":["math:repdigit-product-digits","cnm_019","cnm_p116"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, 81","reason":"111111111² = 12345678987654321. Its digit sum is (1+2+...+9) + (1+2+...+8) = 45 + 36 = 81.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canoni